I am standing in the kitchen in the office.
My colleague Nele comes in.
We take a coffee break and talk about our week.
Nele tells me about her plans for Friday.
"I am cooking a big dinner on Friday," she says.
"I hope that you have time."
"I invite you to my flat."
I am very happy about the invitation.
"That is a great idea," I answer.
"I will definitely come!"
"Perfect!" Nele says cheerfully.
"I will make something delicious."
"Should I bring something?" I ask.
"No, that is not necessary," she answers.
"I will give you my address later."
I finish my coffee and go back to the desk.
I am sure that it will be a great evening.
